---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PRIVACY_LAST_UPDATED } from '../consts';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="SomaFlow collects no personal data. No accounts, no analytics, no ads, no tracking — everything stays on your device."
>
  <article class="my-section">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated: {PRIVACY_LAST_UPDATED}</p>

    <p>
      The short version: <strong>SomaFlow collects no personal data.</strong>
      The long version is below, and it stays short because there genuinely
      isn’t much to say.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-reading">What the app collects</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. SomaFlow has no accounts, no analytics, no ads, and no
      tracking SDKs. We never see your name, your email, or anything about
      how you use the app.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-reading">Where your data lives</h2>
    <p>
      Everything the app creates — your settings, custom breathing
      techniques, and session history — is stored locally on your device
      and never transmitted anywhere. Deleting the app deletes the data.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-reading">Network use</h2>
    <p>
      SomaFlow makes no network requests in normal use.
      <!-- TODO(Anastasia): verify before publishing — if Expo OTA updates are
           enabled, the app periodically fetches update bundles (a code
           download, not a data upload) from Expo's servers. Either keep the
           sentence below or disable OTA updates and delete it. -->
      The one exception: like many apps, it may occasionally download app
      updates from our app-update provider. That is a one-way download of
      code — nothing about you or your usage is sent along with it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-reading">This website</h2>
    <p>
      This site runs no analytics and sets no cookies. The fonts are bundled
      into the site and served from it directly — not pulled from a
      third-party font service — so opening these pages doesn’t reach out to
      anyone else.
      <!-- TODO(Anastasia): confirm this matches the chosen host (some hosts
           add their own logging — that's server-side and fine, but if you
           add anything client-side, update this section in the same change. -->
    </p>
    <p>
      The one exception is the donation button on the
      <a href="/feedback/">feedback page</a>, which uses Stripe to process
      payments. Opening that page loads Stripe’s code, which may set its own
      cookies for fraud prevention. If you don’t open the feedback page, none
      of that runs. Stripe handles your card details — we never see them, and
      their <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy">privacy policy</a> covers
      what they collect.
    </p>
    <p>
      The feedback form is the one place the site takes anything in: what you
      write there — and your email, if you include one — is sent to us through
      our host (Netlify) so we can read it and reply.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-reading">Questions</h2>
    <p>
      If anything here is unclear, ask through the
      <a href="/feedback/">form on the feedback page</a> and we’ll get back
      to you.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
